{"content":[{"c":["JOASH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Abiezrite who lived at Ophrah and the father of Gideon. Joash built an altar to Baal and an image of Asherah, which Gideon later destroyed (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.6.11-31","r":"Judg.6.11-31","rawR":"Judg.6.11-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.6.11-31","value":"Judg.6.11-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 6:11-31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.7.14","r":"Judg.7.14","rawR":"Judg.7.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.7.14","value":"Judg.7.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.13,29-32","r":"Judg.8.13,29-32","rawR":"Judg.8.13,29-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.13,29-32","value":"Judg.8.13,29-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:13, 29-32"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Son of King Ahab of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.26","r":"1Kgs.22.26","rawR":"1Kgs.22.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.26","value":"1Kgs.22.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.18.25","r":"2Chr.18.25","rawR":"2Chr.18.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.18.25","value":"2Chr.18.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 18:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Alternate name for Jehoash, Ahaziah’s son and king of Judah (835–796 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), in ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.11.2-3","r":"2Kgs.11.2-3","rawR":"2Kgs.11.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.11.2-3","value":"2Kgs.11.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kings 11:2-3"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.11","r":"1Chr.3.11","rawR":"1Chr.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.11","value":"1Chr.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 3:11"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jehoash #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Alternate name for Jehoash, Jehoahaz’s son and king of Israel (798–782 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), in ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.13.10-13","r":"2Kgs.13.10-13","rawR":"2Kgs.13.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.13.10-13","value":"2Kgs.13.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kings 13:10-13"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jehoash_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jehoash #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Judahite from the house of Shelah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.22","r":"1Chr.4.22","rawR":"1Chr.4.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.22","value":"1Chr.4.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Second of Beker’s nine sons and a leader in Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.8","r":"1Chr.7.8","rawR":"1Chr.7.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.8","value":"1Chr.7.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Benjamite warrior who supported David at Ziklag (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.3","r":"1Chr.12.3","rawR":"1Chr.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.3","value":"1Chr.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 12:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["8. One of David’s officials (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.28","r":"1Chr.27.28","rawR":"1Chr.27.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.28","value":"1Chr.27.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Joash","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 6:11-31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.6.11-31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.6.11-31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.6.11-31"},{"anchorText":"7:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.7.14","rawQueryValue":"Judg.7.14","sourceRefExact":"Judg.7.14"},{"anchorText":"8:13, 29-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_works